    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3907" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλδαίνω</span></b> , only pres. and
		impf., exc. 
			Ep.
		aor.
		3sg.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤλδᾰνε</span> (v. infr.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλδήσασκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>L.</u>
					370
				</span></i>
			 :—causal of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλδήσκω</span>, <i>make to grow, nourish, strengthen</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλε᾽ ἤλδανε ποιμένι λαῶν</span>
			<i>she filled out</i> his limbs, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.70
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				24.368
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμὸν ἀλδαίνουσαν ἐν εὐφροσύναις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					539
				</span></i>
			; <i>increase, multiply</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃς οὐκ ἐάσει γλῶσσαν . . ἀλδαίνειν
					κακά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					557
				</span></i>
			 :— 
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Aglaïas
				12
			</span></i>.</div>
